# ~2 GiB for a screen that a headless Spark never uses and MemAvailable never counts. With --parallel the pool is
# credited TF_GLM_DISPLAY_KV_MIB of it, and the first DSA layers' latent planes are carved from one span: ordinary host
# memory, then a DRM dumb buffer on /dev/dri/card0 mapped right above it, both registered with cuMemHostRegister, so the
# planes take exactly the credit from the reservation and no more host memory than without it. CUDA refuses a memcpy
# across the two registrations, so the pool's row copies of those planes go through an elementwise kernel. Placement
# only: the same bits. Headless Sparks only: a connected display stops the start. Fails closed. After @gabewillen's
# display-reserve KV for the vLLM kit (MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks#234). By @ezoushen.

